# [[.Name]]

[[.Title]]: [[.Summary]]. Generated by kickhub from `[[.Template]]` v[[.Version]], target **[[.Target]]**.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `internal/handler/handler.go` | `Process(bucket, key)`: your logic goes here |
| `internal/handler/s3event.go` | Parses S3-format notifications |
| `cmd/server` | HTTP receiver for S3-format events, used locally and for replaying events |
[[ if eq .Target "aws" -]]
| `cmd/lambda` | Adapts S3 events to `Process` |
| `infra/` | Bucket, Lambda, notification and a read-only role |
[[- else if eq .Target "gcp" -]]
| `function.go` | Adapts Cloud Storage events to `Process` |
| `infra/` | Bucket, Cloud Function, Eventarc trigger and service account |
[[- else -]]
| `docker-compose.yml` | MinIO wired to post upload events to the handler |
[[- end ]]
| `.kickhub.yaml` | Records the template, version and parameters used |

## Run it
[[ if eq .Target "local" ]]
```sh
make up        # MinIO on :9000, console on :9001, handler on :8080
make upload    # uploads README.md into the bucket
make logs      # the handler logs "object uploaded"
make down
```
[[ else if eq .Target "aws" ]]
```sh
make test
make infra-apply
aws s3 cp README.md "s3://$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw bucket)/README.md"
aws logs tail "/aws/lambda/[[.Name]]" --since 5m
```
[[ else ]]
```sh
make test
make infra-apply
gcloud storage cp README.md "gs://$(terraform -chdir=infra output -raw bucket)/README.md"
gcloud functions logs read [[.Name]] --region [[.P.gcp_region]] --limit 20
```
[[ end ]]
Keep `Process` idempotent: every platform here can deliver the same event twice.
